{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9b856ae6","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.009959,"end_time":"2026-10-22T17:49:44.028731+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-22T17:49:44.018772+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Cross-Asset Volatility Forecasting: Comparing GARCH Models Across Equities and Cryptocurrencies\n","\n","**Objective.** Compare three GARCH family models, GARCH(1,1), EGARCH(1,1) and GJR-GARCH(1,1), for forecasting the daily volatility of six assets: three large cap equities (`AAPL`, `JPM`, `XOM`) and three cryptocurrencies (`BTC-USD`, `ETH-USD`, `SOL-USD`). Volatility measures the size of price swings and is a key input to risk management.\n","\n","**Research questions**\n","\n","1. Is volatility more persistent in equities or in cryptocurrencies?\n","2. Do asymmetric models (EGARCH and GJR-GARCH) outperform standard GARCH, and does this depend on the asset class?\n","3. Does the model with the best in sample fit (AIC) also give the best out of sample forecasts?\n","\n","**Approach**\n","\n","| Stage | Description |\n","|---|---|\n","| Data collection | Five years of daily prices for all six assets through one reusable extraction class |\n","| Storage | One SQLite table per asset, read back to compute daily returns |\n","| Exploration | Prices, returns, volatility clustering and autocorrelation of returns and squared returns |\n","| Modelling | Three specifications fitted to each asset on the first 80% of its returns (18 models) |\n","| Comparison | AIC and BIC, volatility persistence, asymmetry parameters and residual diagnostics |\n","| Validation | Walk forward, one day ahead forecasts on the last 20%, scored with RMSE and QLIKE |\n","\n","**Data.** Daily OHLCV data from Yahoo Finance through `yfinance`, with adjusted prices. Returns are daily percentage changes of the closing price. The data is downloaded when the notebook runs, so results change slightly with the download date.\n","\n","**Requirements.** Internet access for package installation and Yahoo Finance, and no GPU. The walk forward step refits every model at every test day and is the slow part. It can take tens of minutes on the full test window.\n","\n","**Contents**\n","\n","1. Setup\n","2. Data collection\n","3. Data storage and returns\n","4. Exploratory data analysis\n","5. Train/test split\n","6. GARCH modelling\n","7. Model comparison and diagnostics\n","8. Walk forward validation\n","9. Summary"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0c42cfb2","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.008975,"end_time":"2026-10-22T17:49:44.046295+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-22T17:49:44.03732+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Step 1: Setup"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"25369259","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-22T17:49:44.063983Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-22T17:49:44.063161Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-22T17:49:50.193711Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-22T17:49:50.192641Z"},"papermill":{"duration":6.141436,"end_time":"2026-10-22T17:49:50.195631+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-22T17:49:44.054195+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Collecting arch\r\n","  Downloading arch-8.0.0-cp312-cp312-manylinux2014_x86_64.manylinux_2_17_x86_64.manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl.metadata (13 kB)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: numpy<3,>=1.22.3 in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from arch) (2.0.2)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: pandas>=1.4.0 in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from arch) (2.3.3)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: scipy>=1.8 in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from arch) (1.16.3)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: statsmodels>=0.13.0 in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from arch) (0.14.6)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied: packaging in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from arch) (26.1)\r\n","Requirement already satisfied